          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On July 3, 2012, around 9:15 PM, a driver observes a phenomenon that intrigues him: two spheres separated by something resembling a rotating helix move across the cloudy sky. The phenomenon is of dark gray color and is not equipped with position lights. From his vehicle, the witness, a former pilot, does not recognize the object. No other testimonies will be collected. After an in-depth investigation, no satisfactory hypothesis was retained (see the investigation report). In conclusion, although the witness shows great credibility, a flawless hearing and reconstruction, this observation case lacks information and additional testimonies; it remains of average consistency. The strangeness of the case is also average as plausible hypotheses can be found, but they could not be neither validated nor refuted. The GEIPAN classifies this case as 'C' due to lack of information and cross-referencing.",
